<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>WhimprFlow uses your microphone to transcribe what you say into text.</string>

    <!--
      Menu-bar app, not a Dock app — the shape Amphetamine and Grammarly have.
      A dictation tool is reached by holding a key inside some OTHER app, so a Dock
      tile is a permanent slot spent on an icon nobody clicks.

      Declared here rather than left to `set_activation_policy(Accessory)` at
      runtime, which was tried first and is not sufficient on its own: LaunchServices
      fixes the application type from this file at launch, so the app came up as a
      Foreground app with a Dock tile — `lsappinfo` reported `ApplicationType =
      "Foreground"` and System Events `background only = false` — before any Rust
      had run. The runtime call stays as well, because it is what gives `cargo run`
      the same behavior without a bundle.

      Consequence worth knowing: with no Dock tile, the tray's "Open WhimprFlow" is
      the ONLY way back to the Hub, which is why closing the Hub must hide it rather
      than destroy it. See `CloseRequested` in lib.rs.
    -->
    <key>LSUIElement</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
